feat(subscriptions): complete pro-subscription infrastructure, INACTIVE behind PAYMENTS_ENABLED (admin-only)

Builds everything needed to charge professionals later (₡3.000/mes, ₡30.000/año
= 2 meses gratis) WITHOUT activating or exposing it now. With the flag off
(default) regular users see zero payment/subscription UI; admin management is the
only visible surface (for testing the manual SINPE flow).

- Feature flag: NEXT_PUBLIC_PAYMENTS_ENABLED (default false) in lib/payments/config.ts
  (+ plans/prices/cycles, SINPE placeholder, formatColones).
- DB (migration 054 — apply in Supabase): `subscriptions` (one per pro) +
  `subscription_payments` ledger. RLS = owner-read only; all writes via
  service-role (admin APIs / webhooks). NEVER stores card data (gateway refs only).
- Backend (lib/payments/subscriptions.ts, server-only via admin client):
  isSubscriptionActive, computePeriodEnd (monthly/annual), priceForCycle,
  get/ensure subscription + payments, activatePaidPeriod (records payment + sets
  active + extends), setSubscriptionStatus.
- Gateway abstraction (lib/payments/gateway.ts): PaymentGateway interface + Stub
  (throws "not integrated"); clear integration points for ONVO/Tilopay. Raw card
  data never touches our server/DB.
- APIs: /api/payments/subscription (pro self GET/POST — returns enabled:false &
  refuses checkout while off), /api/payments/webhook (inert until wired),
  /api/admin/subscriptions (admin-only: GET status+history, POST manual activate/
  extend/deactivate — SINPE flow).
- Pro UI (hidden): subscription-panel.tsx mounted only via a "Suscripción" tab
  that exists ONLY when PAYMENTS_ENABLED; content branch double-guarded.
- Admin UI (visible now, admin-only): AdminSubscription in the admin user profile
  — status, manual SINPE activate/extend/deactivate, payment history.

To activate later: apply migration 054, plug a gateway in gateway.ts, set the real
SINPE number, update the legal pages, set NEXT_PUBLIC_PAYMENTS_ENABLED=true.

